From: vedcsolution <vedcsolution@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 540/540] [DS4.1] SP row exchange tests at five and six ranks

The sequence-parallel row exchange and PyNCCL's all_to_all_rows only relay
at four ranks (the switchless ring); every other rank count sends each peer
its block directly. Their tests covered three and four ranks; they now also
run five and six, the switch's TP5 and TP6, with the last blocks short or
empty as before. No code changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../models/test_deepseek_v41_sp_project_reduce_scatter.py  | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/models/test_deepseek_v41_sp_project_reduce_scatter.py b/tests/models/test_deepseek_v41_sp_project_reduce_scatter.py
index 1a2c9c4..c9851fe 100644
--- a/tests/models/test_deepseek_v41_sp_project_reduce_scatter.py
+++ b/tests/models/test_deepseek_v41_sp_project_reduce_scatter.py
@@ -278,7 +278,7 @@ def test_moe_combine_writes_the_exchange_slots(
 
 
 @pytest.mark.parametrize("tokens", [37, 40, 205])
-@pytest.mark.parametrize("world", [3, 4])
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("world", [3, 4, 5, 6])
 def test_row_exchange_gives_each_rank_its_rows_of_every_block(
     monkeypatch, tokens, world
 ):
@@ -355,13 +355,14 @@ class _Fabric:
         self.barrier.wait()
 
 
-@pytest.mark.parametrize("world", [3, 4])
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("world", [3, 4, 5, 6])
 @pytest.mark.parametrize("short", [0, 3, 9, 10, 25])
 def test_row_all_to_all_over_cabled_pairs(world, short, rows=10):
     """PyNCCL's ``all_to_all_rows``, every rank a thread: each rank receives every
     rank's block of its real rows bit for bit and later rows stay unwritten, with the
     last blocks short or empty; at four ranks (the switchless ring) only neighbours
-    exchange, since ranks two apart share no cable."""
+    exchange, since ranks two apart share no cable; other rank counts (three on a
+    triangle, five and six on a switch) exchange with every peer directly."""
     total = max(1, world * rows - short)
     fabric = _Fabric(world)
     inputs = [torch.randn(total, 6) for _ in range(world)]
